# Shell scripts run inside WSL — they must keep LF endings even when this repo
# is checked out on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. CRLF would break the bash
# shebang / parsing of fak/test.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Golden fixtures are compared BYTE-FOR-BYTE against `\n`-marshaled JSON
# (e.g. internal/abi TestABIGoldenFreeze does `string(want) != string(gotJSON)`).
# Under core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF and the
# byte compare fails locally while passing on Linux/CI. Pin LF so the freeze
# tests are platform-independent.
*.golden text eol=lf

# CUDA reference producers are PROVENANCE-PINNED by SHA-256 (internal/kvint2eval/testdata,
# docs/research/quantization/int2-kv-rotation.md), and a digest only names one artifact if every
# checkout holds the same bytes. Under core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout would rewrite these
# to CRLF and hash differently from the recorded pin — the same failure the *.golden line above
# prevents, so pin LF for the same reason (#6260).
*.cu text eol=lf

# The preregistered harness-control task is SHA-256 addressed; preserve its exact bytes on every OS (#7252).
docs/benchmarks/harness-control-study/task-card.md text eol=lf
docs/benchmarks/harness-control-study/materials/*/task-card.md text eol=lf
docs/benchmarks/harness-control-study/materials/default-control/kernel-component.txt text eol=lf
docs/benchmarks/harness-control-study/README.md text eol=lf

# Copied upstream excerpts are SHA-256 addressed by borrow-provenance tests.
# Pin repository LF bytes so one digest names the artifact on every OS.
internal/canon/testdata/token_usage/upstream/*.txt text eol=lf
internal/modelroute/testdata/provider_contracts/upstream/*.txt text eol=lf

# The new-model replay ledger is generated and compared byte-for-byte; keep its
# canonical JSON line endings stable under core.autocrlf=true (#9570).
internal/newmodel/testdata/replay/ledger.json text eol=lf

# Effective-instruction fixtures and their receipt are SHA-256 addressed; keep
# one byte sequence across autocrlf-enabled Windows and Unix checkouts (#10157).
internal/agentsindex/testdata/effective/** text eol=lf

# The red-team floor report is generated and compared byte-for-byte; keep its
# markdown line endings stable under core.autocrlf=true (#11345).
internal/policy/testdata/redteam_floor_report.md text eol=lf
